.TH KEYRING-SECURE 1 "September 2025" "MyWallet Toolkit 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
keyring-secure \- production-hardened secure private key management daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keyring-secure.sh
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-a
.IR action ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR label ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR timeout ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keyring-secure.sh
is a production-hardened secure keyring daemon that manages Bitcoin private keys in memory with automatic timeout and comprehensive security features. It implements defense-in-depth security with multiple protection layers against various attack vectors.

The keyring daemon stores private keys only in secure memory (shared memory when available), never writing them to disk. Keys are automatically expired after a configurable timeout period and are securely wiped from memory using multiple-pass deletion.

.B PRODUCTION SECURITY FEATURES:
.IP \(bu 4
Cryptographically secure 256-bit session IDs
.IP \(bu 4
Shared memory storage (/dev/shm when available)
.IP \(bu 4
Multiple-pass secure deletion (3 passes with random data)
.IP \(bu 4
Atomic file operations with exclusive locking
.IP \(bu 4
Comprehensive input validation and sanitization
.IP \(bu 4
Race condition prevention with proper synchronization
.IP \(bu 4
Memory clearing on timeout/exit with cleanup handlers

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet mode. Suppress informational output.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose mode. Show detailed operations and security status.
.TP
.B \-a \fIaction\fR
Specify action to perform. Available actions:
.RS
.TP
.B status
Show keyring daemon status (default)
.TP
.B auth
Authenticate and store private key in memory
.TP
.B get
Retrieve stored private key (for scripts)
.TP
.B clear
Clear stored keys and reset timeout
.TP
.B kill
Stop keyring daemon
.RE
.TP
.B \-l \fIlabel\fR
Key label/identifier (alphanumeric + underscore, max 32 chars, default: "default")
.TP
.B \-t \fItimeout\fR
Timeout in seconds (1-300, default: 60)
.TP
.B \-h
Show help message and exit.

.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B status
Display current daemon status including number of cached keys, time remaining, and security configuration. Shows whether secure storage (tmpfs) is active.
.TP
.B auth
Prompt for private key and store it securely in memory. The key is validated for format correctness (64 hexadecimal characters) before storage.
.TP
.B get
Retrieve a previously stored private key. Used by other scripts in the toolkit. Returns empty if key expired or not found.
.TP
.B clear
Immediately clear all cached keys and reset timeout. Keys are securely wiped with multiple passes of random data.
.TP
.B kill
Stop the keyring daemon and perform complete cleanup of all secure storage areas.

.SH SECURITY ARCHITECTURE
.SS Memory Protection
The keyring uses multiple layers of memory protection:
.IP \(bu 4
Shared memory storage (/dev/shm) when available for RAM-only operations
.IP \(bu 4
Secure file permissions (600/700) for all temporary files
.IP \(bu 4
Multiple-pass secure deletion using random data overwriting
.IP \(bu 4
Automatic memory clearing on process exit or signal handling

.SS Input Validation
All inputs undergo comprehensive validation:
.IP \(bu 4
Label names restricted to alphanumeric characters plus underscore and hyphen
.IP \(bu 4
Maximum label length enforced (32 characters)
.IP \(bu 4
Private key format validation (exactly 64 hexadecimal characters)
.IP \(bu 4
Timeout bounds checking (1-300 seconds)

.SS Process Isolation
Security isolation features include:
.IP \(bu 4
Cryptographically secure session IDs (256-bit entropy)
.IP \(bu 4
Process-specific temporary directories
.IP \(bu 4
Exclusive file locking to prevent race conditions
.IP \(bu 4
Signal handlers for proper cleanup on termination

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Show keyring status:
.B keyring-secure.sh -a status
.TP
Store private key with verbose output:
.B keyring-secure.sh -v -a auth
.TP
Store key with custom label and timeout:
.B keyring-secure.sh -a auth -l wallet1 -t 120
.TP
Retrieve stored key (for scripts):
.B keyring-secure.sh -q -a get -l wallet1
.TP
Clear all cached keys:
.B keyring-secure.sh -a clear
.TP
Stop daemon completely:
.B keyring-secure.sh -a kill

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BITCOIN_SESSION_ID
Session identifier. Auto-generated with cryptographic entropy if not set.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/shm/.bitcoin-keyring-*
Secure shared memory storage directory (when available)
.TP
.I /tmp/.bitcoin-keyring-*
Fallback temporary storage directory

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution
.TP
.B 1
Authentication failed, invalid input, or system error

.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.IP \(bu 4
Never run as root - the script includes checks to prevent privilege escalation
.IP \(bu 4
Keys are stored only in memory, never written to persistent storage
.IP \(bu 4
Automatic timeout prevents long-term key exposure
.IP \(bu 4
Multiple security layers protect against various attack vectors
.IP \(bu 4
Production-hardened for enterprise environments

.SH INTEGRATION
This secure keyring integrates with other toolkit components:
.IP \(bu 4
